---
description: Reconcile an installed worker package with its actual reviewed authority and explain the resulting supported verification scope.
args:
  goal: string
returns: InstalledPackageOutcome
---
Help the operator resolve the installed-package question in the goal. Use investigateInstalledPackage to establish the assigned worker, actual local declaration and protected baseline before deciding what is justified. A healthy live service is not proof that a differently named local package or changed review scope is authorized.

Decide whether the user requests a restoration or an inspection. If an actual restoration is requested and supported by the exact observed review, use restorePackage with the computed observation. Preserve a refusal, changed revision, withdrawn grant or foreign identity as evidence; do not manufacture a successful edit or retry an old approval on a new state. The native port alone performs the exact scoped change and preserves unrelated fields.

A declaration differing from its protected baseline can still own its current suite plan. Compare the actual source, suite name and working runtime; neither baseline equality nor a restore grant is required to report an admitted current inspection.

Use reviewVerification when the user's question needs the current declared suite or runner. Pass the actual latest observation, including a restore response when present. This is plan inspection, not permission to open a panel, run a file, rebuild a worker or contact a provider.

Return the useful domain finding in natural language, including every requested explanation, supported suite or remaining evidence gap. Distinguish an authorized completed restoration from an unsupported proposal and from the current verification plan. Use the actual computed values in composition rather than reconstructing opaque revision or receipt fields.
